 "note": "Appendix §H, \"A failed revocation write\". c1 executes P1 and queues P2 and P3. It loses control and the fence write itself fails (the rollback succeeds). In the same step the host revokes the lease in memory (revoked to c2; its epoch isn't persisted, so the fixture doesn't name it), rejects P2 and P3 in memory (control revoked; no live attachment of c1 is entitled to the receipts, so nothing is sent), halts the journal and closes c1's new link without a welcome (only c2 stays attached). P1's turn ending dispatches nothing: nothing queued is dispatched after a halt, and c2's Send is busy. A halted run writes no clean close, so after the restart P2 and P3 are durably rejected (authorization history unknown) before anything is dispatched, P1 is outcome_unknown, and nothing ever runs again."
}
